		{"id":"c9d2bf614d702e31","type":"text","text":"1. overall structure of information changed\n2. Intent should change accordingly \n    1. intents are biased toward goodday\n    2. product information hardcode removal from system prompt\n3. agentic behaviour (ReaAct Nature) \n    1. multi product ask (future but baseline is necessary)\n4. Output response format. with recommendation.","x":2621,"y":1559,"width":650,"height":290},
		{"id":"186b02593f4ad52d","type":"text","text":"1. Intent classification correction\n\t1. design the flow\n\t2. list the intents\n\t\t1. general\n\t\t2. out of scope\n\t\t3. granular progress\n\t\t\t1. daily information\n\t\t4. weekly progress\n\t3. correlation should be there between the daily and weekly information","x":3440,"y":1768,"width":700,"height":300},
		{
			"id":"84d5d69b43736ea6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## questions Aug - 13\n\n**1. Best cross-product test**\n\n> **“I want to introduce a new initiative that integrates Kruise Workflow with the IIP/ERP system. Based on the work happening since August 10, what risks, gaps, dependencies, and delivery conflicts would this new initiative introduce?”**\n\n**2. New work inside Kruise**\n\n> **“I want to introduce a new requirement in Kruise Workflow: workflows should support reliable scheduled execution in production. Given the work already happening, what new risks and gaps would this introduce, and what existing work does it depend on?”**\n\n**3. New work inside IIP**\n\n> **“I want to introduce a new ERP requirement for an end-to-end automated Stock receiving workflow. Looking at the current IIP work, what existing work would this depend on, and what new risks or gaps would it create?”**\n\n**4. New priority competing with existing work**\n\n> **“If I make a new Kruise Workflow–ERP integration a top priority, what existing work in IIP and Kruise could be affected, and what risks or bottlenecks should I expect?”**\n\n**5. CEO decision question**\n\n> **“I am considering approving a new cross-product initiative between IIP/ERP and Kruise Workflow. Before I approve it, tell me what existing work it would depend on, what risks and gaps it introduces, and whether there is anything already in progress that could make this a bad time to start.”**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1900,
			"y":1905,
			"width":960,
			"height":670
		},
		{
			"id":"b66a92aea42fd728",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Available tools today:\n\n- `search_knowledge` / `get_knowledge_document` (indexed docs)\n- `read_enterprise_knowledge` / `read_enterprise_knowledge_item` (Teams daily reports)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-2780,
			"y":3460,
			"width":700,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"4d051a511c115f50",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"### `search_knowledge`\n\nTold to the model: semantic search over indexed knowledge — Azure Blob department reports, daily Teams fetch, PMO weekly uploads. Use for status, weekly reports, milestones, timelines. Returns cited chunks. Optional `source`: `teams` | `upload`.\n\nWhat it actually does: vector search in Qdrant, then lexical/temporal rerank. It searches already indexed docs (uploads + Teams reports copied into the knowledge index). It is not a live Teams fetch.\n\nAccuracy: directionally right, but incomplete in ways that affect tool choice:\n\n- It does not say Teams daily reports are also in this index, so it overlaps with enterprise tools\n- `product_key` exists in the Python function but is not in the schema and is never passed from `_execute_tool_call`\n- It does not say empty query → empty result, or that `top_k` defaults from RAG settings\n\n### `get_knowledge_document`\n\nTold to the model: metadata plus a short structural overview (first/last chunks) by `document_id` or blob `source_ref`.\n\nWhat it actually does: first 3 chunks and last 3 chunks, each truncated to 400 characters. Not the full document.\n\nAccuracy: good. The name sounds like “read the doc,” which can make a model skip `search_knowledge` and call this too early without an id.\n\n### `read_enterprise_knowledge`\n\nTold to the model: list stored Enterprise Knowledge — daily Teams reports, one markdown file per product group per day, as of last Fetch. Returns id (blob path) + short preview. Use for daily updates / blockers / task status. Then call the item tool.\n\nWhat it actually does: lists the last snapshot, max 20 reports, with id, title, product, date, snippet. Org-wide in chat (`product_key` is never passed). Not live Graph.\n\nAccuracy: mostly right. Gaps:\n\n- Cap of 20 is not mentioned\n- “Call this only when you need real org context” is vague and can suppress it on status questions\n- Overlap with `search_knowledge` (source=`teams`) is not explained\n\n### `read_enterprise_knowledge_item`\n\nTold to the model: read the full body of one daily Teams report by id from the list tool.\n\nWhat it actually does: returns that report, truncated to 6000 characters.\n\nAccuracy: almost right, except “full body” is not always full.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
